GateKeeper applications should use a **backend-for-frontend (BFF)** integration whenever the
framework has a server runtime. Tokens stay server-side, the browser receives only an encrypted
`httpOnly` session cookie, and the application calls GateKeeper through a small framework-specific
adapter. `@gatekeeper/sveltekit-bff`, `@gatekeeper/nextjs`, and `@gatekeeper/remix` are all
**confidential** clients of this kind — they hold a client secret on the server.

Browser-only frameworks sit on the other side of that boundary. A single-page app cannot keep a
secret, so it registers as a **public** OAuth client: no client secret, PKCE S256 as the only
client protection, and tokens that live in the browser (`sessionStorage`), exposed to XSS by design.
`@gatekeeper/react`, `@gatekeeper/vue`, `@gatekeeper/angular`, `@gatekeeper/angularjs`, and the
framework-agnostic `@gatekeeper/browser` are public clients.

> **Public clients require a public OAuth client.** Register each SPA with `client_type: "public"`
> and **no client secret**, and add its dev origin to the server's `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (the SPA
> calls `/oauth/token` and `/oauth/userinfo` directly from the browser). Prefer a confidential BFF
> whenever the framework has a server runtime.

## Shared cores

To avoid re-implementing security-sensitive OAuth logic per framework, the adapters build on two
framework-agnostic cores:

- **`@gatekeeper/spa-oauth`** — the public Authorization Code + PKCE browser client (subscribable
  state machine, `sessionStorage` tokens, silent refresh). React, Vue, Angular, and AngularJS are
  thin idiomatic bindings over it.
- **`@gatekeeper/bff-core`** — the confidential BFF core (AES-256-GCM `httpOnly` session cookie,
  refresh-token rotation with coalescing). Next.js and Remix bind their route/loader idioms to it.

The repository keeps every adapter as a downloadable package under `packages/`. The website docs
track them through a small catalog in `website/src/lib/docs/framework-libraries.ts`, so adding a
new framework later follows the same shape instead of becoming a one-off docs change.

